ing defined (the quota enforcement work), since the quota-consumption view builds against it.\" Body must not name E002. I'll add a \"Dependencies\" line in description or scope: \"Builds against the per-project GPU quota model established by the quota-enforcement work; runs in parallel with the admission and preemption tracks (it reads existing Kubernetes/queueing APIs).\" Good.\n\n---\n\n**E007 body** (topology investigation):\n\nTitle: Assess maturity of node topology discovery for topology-aware placement\n\nDescription: Resolves the strategy's open question for HLR-5: whether node topology discovery (currently Tech Preview) is mature enough to build topology-aware job placement on in this release.\n\nScope:\n- Assess the current state of node topology discovery (API stability, known issues, upgrade behavior, support status) from public/upstream documentation, release notes, and issue trackers.\n- Validate actual topology reporting on representative GPU node topologies (e.g. NVLink domains) where hardware is available.\n- Determine compatibility with the platform's queueing/scheduling stack.\n- Produce a bounded decision: (A) mature enough — proceed with topology-aware placement this release; (B) not mature enough — defer HLR-5.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n- A written assessment with a clear go/no-go decision for building on topology discovery this release.\n- Evidence cited (API versions, known issues, support status) sufficient to justify the decision.\n- If no-go: a summary of what maturity gaps exist and what would change the decision.\n\nHLR Traceability: HLR-5 (P2) — resolves the gating unknown for topology-aware placement.\n\n---\n\n**BRANCH-A-E003 body**:\n\nTitle: Kueue-native gang admission for multi-node training jobs\n\nDescription: Implements HLR-1 using Kueue's native all-or-nothing admission (waitForPodsReady), selected when the gang-admission validation confirms Kueue semantics are sufficient at target scale. Multi-node training jobs are admitted al