configurable without code changes.\n\nHLR Traceability: HLR-4 (P1) — full coverage (eviction+requeue path).\n\ngate_failure_impact: rewrite, fallback=\"If the required semantics are checkpoint-aware graceful preemption, this epic is rewritten as graceful preemption on the queueing side plus training-side checkpoint hooks.\"\n\n---\n\n**BRANCH-B-E005 body**:\n\nTitle: Checkpoint-aware graceful preemption — queueing side\n\nDescription: Implements the queueing side of HLR-4 with checkpoint-aware graceful preemption semantics: when a higher-priority workload preempts a lower-priority training job, the job is signaled to checkpoint and is stopped gracefully, then requeued and restored on re-admission. Selected when the preemption-semantics investigation chooses graceful semantics.\n\nScope:\n- Graceful preemption mechanism in the queueing layer: on preemption, notify the workload to checkpoint, allow a bounded grace period, then complete eviction; requeue for re-admission.\n- Admin-defined preemption policy (priority scheme, preemptability) as in the eviction-based path.\n- Integration of the grace/checkpoint protocol with per-project quota on re-admission.\n- May require upstream Kueue contribution if native hooks are insufficient — coordinate accordingly.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n- On preemption per admin-defined policy, a training job receives a checkpoint signal and a bounded grace period before eviction (HLR-4).\n- The preempted job is requeued and, on re-admission, resumes from its checkpoint.\n- Checkpoint overhead stays within the bounds characterized by the preemption-semantics investigation.\n- Policy is admin-configurable.\n\nHLR Traceability: HLR-4 (P1) — queueing-side coverage (graceful path).\n\ngate_failure_impact: rewrite, fallback=\"If the required semantics are full eviction with requeue, this epic is rewritten as the simpler eviction+requeue preemption policy.\"\n\nDependencies: the preemption-semantics investigation (E004) + per-project quota model (