eduler-plugin\n  alternative (e.g. coscheduling) — what integration with the platform scheduler and the\n  Kueue quota/admission model would be required.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written assessment exists answering the open question for both PyTorchJob and RayJob,\n  with reproducible evidence (test configurations, measurements, environment details).\n- The assessment states a clear bounded decision per job type: (A) Kueue-native\n  waitForPodsReady semantics are sufficient, or (B) scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue\n  is required.\n- The decision criterion is explicit and measurable (no partial GPU occupation beyond a\n  bounded admission timeout at target scale).\n- If outcome B: the gap analysis is detailed enough to scope the scheduler-plugin\n  integration work without a second discovery pass.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): resolves the gating unknown for all-or-nothing admission of multi-node\n  training jobs; the chosen implementation path (Kueue-native vs scheduler-plugin) is\n  selected by this investigation's outcome.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52513,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0fc9485f8eba266","agent_id":"a81a7a1b3aa452de0","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"6aaab0bc-357c-48a8-bcc0-2e4e79c41825","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:31:22.241Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
