{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1dd4a793-1b23-422d-9879-d20cef8c336b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d674866ecc5b600","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-qprkorub/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-E002.md","content":"# Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission for training workloads\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers HLR-2: per-project GPU quota is enforced at admission time across training job\ntypes (PyTorchJob, RayJob). Built on the platform's existing Kueue-based queueing model\n(ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model per the Distributed Workloads architecture context).\nA job whose project has exhausted its GPU quota is queued rather than partially scheduled.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define and implement the per-project GPU quota model for training workloads using the\n  existing Kueue quota machinery (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue).\n- Ensure both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads are subject to queue admission and counted\n  against their project's GPU quota — PyTorchJob via the existing Kueue integration;\n  RayJob via the kuberay integration (validate and close any gaps so both job types are\n  quota-subject).\n- Administrative configuration of per-project GPU quota values without code changes.\n- Incidental documentation updates that fall out of this change (quota configuration\n  references) are included here as scope; no separate documentation work stream.\n\nThis work is independent of the gang-admission semantics question (all-or-nothing\nadmission): quota enforcement applies at Kueue admission either way, so it proceeds in\nparallel with that investigation and its follow-on implementation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A job submitted to a project whose GPU quota is exhausted is not admitted (remains\n  pending in queue) rather than partially scheduled — for both PyTorchJob and RayJob\n  (HLR-2).\n- Quota consumption accounts for GPU resources across both training job types within a\n  project (a PyTorchJob and a RayJob in the same project draw from the same quota).\n- Demonstrated test: an over-quota job stays queued while quota is held by admitted jobs;\n  when capacity is released, the pending job is admitted.\n- Per-project GPU quota is configurable by an administrator without code changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P0): full coverage — per-project GPU quota enforced at admission time across\n  training job types.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":53256,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0fc9485f8eba266","agent_id":"a81a7a1b3aa452de0","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"68539070-c3ab-43cc-9891-4935a16667fb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:31:34.335Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
