{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1e928650-76a0-4abf-a0d4-7fff195d56fd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8ca9f59564e08c9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9005-qprkorub/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E003.md","content":"# Kueue-native gang admission for multi-node training jobs\n\n## Description\n\nImplements HLR-1 using Kueue's native all-or-nothing admission (waitForPodsReady),\nselected when the gang-admission validation investigation confirms Kueue semantics are\nsufficient at target scale. Multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing: no\npartial GPU occupation while waiting for the remaining pods.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Enable and configure Kueue's waitForPodsReady gang-admission semantics for PyTorchJob\n  and RayJob workloads (admission timeout, pods-ready conditions) per the validation\n  findings.\n- Tune admission timeout and requeue behavior for partially-ready jobs so they do not\n  hold GPUs indefinitely (the problem statement's \"12 of 16 GPUs held for hours\" failure\n  mode).\n- Rollback path: because this replaces the existing piecemeal admission behavior, the\n  all-or-nothing semantics must be revertible per-queue via configuration (feature-flag /\n  rollback requirement).\n- Validation at target scale reproducing the validation investigation's decision\n  criterion for both job types.\n- Incidental documentation updates that fall out of this change are included here as\n  scope; no separate documentation work stream.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A multi-node PyTorchJob (e.g. 16-GPU class) is admitted all-or-nothing: while pending,\n  it holds zero GPUs — no partial GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods\n  (HLR-1).\n- The same all-or-nothing guarantee holds for RayJob workloads.\n- Partially-unready jobs are evicted and requeued within the configured timeout rather\n  than holding GPUs for hours.\n- Admission semantics can be reverted per-queue via configuration without platform\n  reinstall (rollback / feature flag).\n- Scheduling of non-training workloads is unaffected.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): full coverage on the Kueue-native path (applies when the gang-admission\n  validation selects this outcome).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":55603,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0fc9485f8eba266","agent_id":"a81a7a1b3aa452de0","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"b3b3d159-0448-4839-8d0e-603684c565b6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:32:21.387Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9005"}
