{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99ade77a041a331a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n3\tepic_count: 11\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9005: Queue-aware GPU scheduling for distributed training workloads\n11\t\n12\tStrategy status: Refinement Done; priority: Critical. Full decomposition (not triaged):\n13\tthe strategy spans three components (Distributed Workloads, Training Operator, Dashboard),\n14\ttwo teams, and five HLRs across P0–P2, with three open questions that gate the shape of\n15\timplementation work.\n16\t\n17\t## Epic List\n18\t\n19\tMain-plan epics (5):\n20\t\n21\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n22\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E001 | Validate Kueue gang admission for multi-node training jobs at target scale | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E002 | Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission for training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E004 | Determine required preemption semantics and checkpoint overhead | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E006 | Dashboard visibility for queue position, quota consumption, and admission state | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-E007 | Assess maturity of node topology discovery for topology-aware placement | Investigation | Distributed Workloads | P2 |\n28\t\n29\tBranch epics (6, conditional — plan documents attached to their gating Investigation, not\n30\tstandalone Jira issues):\n31\t\n32\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Branch condition |\n33\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|------------------|\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E003 | Kueue-native gang admission for multi-node training jobs | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | A: Kueue waitForPodsReady sufficient at target scale |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E003 | Coscheduling scheduler-plugin integration for gang admission | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P0 | B: scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue required |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E005 | Kueue preemption policy with full eviction and requeue | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 | A: full-eviction semantics chosen |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E005 | Checkpoint-aware graceful preemption — queueing side | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 | B: checkpoint-aware graceful semantics chosen |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E006 | PyTorchJob checkpoint hooks for graceful preemption | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 | B: checkpoint-aware graceful semantics chosen |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008 | Topology-aware job placement for GPU training workloads | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P2 | A: topology discovery mature enough this release |\n40\t\n41\tTotals: 11 epics (5 main-plan + 6 branch). `epic_count` counts all epics including branches.\n42\t\n43\t## Dependency DAG\n44\t\n45\t```mermaid\n46\tgraph TD\n47\t    E001[\"E001 Inv: Kueue gang admission validation (P0)\"]\n48\t    E002[\"E002 Impl: Per-project GPU quota (P0)\"]\n49\t    E004[\"E004 Inv: Preemption semantics + checkpoint benchmark (P1)\"]\n50\t    E006[\"E006 Impl: Dashboard queue/quota/admission views (P1)\"]\n51\t    E007[\"E007 Inv: Topology discovery maturity (P2)\"]\n52\t\n53\t    E002 --> E006\n54\t\n55\t    A003[\"Branch A - E003: Kueue-native gang admission\"]\n56\t    B003[\"Branch B - E003: Coscheduling plugin integration\"]\n57\t    E001 --> A003\n58\t    E001 --> B003\n59\t\n60\t    A005[\"Branch A - E005: Eviction+requeue preemption\"]\n61\t    B005[\"Branch B - E005: Graceful preemption, queueing side\"]\n62\t    B006[\"Branch B - E006: PyTorchJob checkpoint hooks\"]\n63\t    E004 --> A005\n64\t    E004 --> B005\n65\t    E002 --> A005\n66\t    E002 --> B005\n67\t    B005 --> B006\n68\t\n69\t    A008[\"Branch A - E008: Topology-aware placement\"]\n70\t    E007 --> A008\n71\t```\n72\t\n73\tMain-plan critical path: E002 → E006 (length 2, counting nodes). Branch epics are excluded\n74\tfrom the main-plan critical path per convention; the longest branch-inclusive chain would be\n75\tE002 → BRANCH-B-E005 → BRANCH-B-E006 (3 nodes).\n76\t\n77\t## DAG Justification\n78\t\n79\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n80\t|------|------|-----------|\n81\t| E002 → E006 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The Dashboard's quota-consumption view builds against the per-project quota/queue model the quota epic establishes; serializing avoids rework if the model's shape changes. The Dashboard otherwise reads existing Kubernetes CRs and queueing surfaces and runs parallel to the admission, preemption, and topology tracks (Rule 14, different repos, no shared artifact). |\n82\t| E001 ⟶ BRANCH-A/B-E003 (gate) | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | Open question 1 decides whether HLR-1 is delivered Kueue-natively or via scheduler-plugin work — the strategy states the answer \"changes the shape of most implementation work\". Two bounded outcomes → conditional branches. |\n83\t| E004 ⟶ BRANCH-A/B-E005, BRANCH-B-E006 (gate) | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | Open question 3 decides whether HLR-4 preemption is full eviction with requeue or checkpoint-aware graceful preemption; the latter adds a Training Operator checkpoint-hooks epic. Two bounded outcomes → conditional branches. |\n84\t| E002 → BRANCH-A/B-E005 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The preemption policy is defined on the per-project quota/queue model; preemption work is a consumer of that model. |\n85\t| BRANCH-B-E005 → BRANCH-B-E006 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer, within branch B) | The training-side checkpoint hooks implement the graceful-preemption protocol defined by the queueing-side work in the same branch. |\n86\t| E007 ⟶ BRANCH-A-E008 (gate) | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | Open question 2 decides whether HLR-5 is built this release (branch A) or deferred (branch B — no epics; HLR-5 descoped). |\n87\t\n88\tNotable non-edges (deliberate):\n89\t\n90\t- E001 ∥ E002 (Rule 15): per-project quota enforcement is independent of gang-admission\n91\t  semantics; both are Kueue-side but separate concerns in the same area boundary.\n92\t- E006 ∥ admission branches (Rule 14): different repos; the Dashboard reads existing CRs and\n93\t  queueing status via the Kubernetes API (per Dashboard architecture context) and shares no\n94\t  artifact with the admission work. End-to-end integration is enforced by an acceptance\n95\t  criterion on the Dashboard epic, not a DAG edge.\n96\t- E001 ∥ E004 ∥ E007: three independent unknowns resolved by different experiments — not\n97\t  combined (each gates a different HLR and produces a different deliverable).\n98\t- No repo-onboarding / konflux-onboarding / license-validation epics: all three components\n99\t  exist in architecture context and are Konflux-onboarded (Rule 20 does not apply).\n100\t- No docs-authoring epic: the strategy declares no documentation support and no Documentation\n101\t  component is affected; incidental documentation updates are folded into the originating\n102\t  epics as scope/acceptance criteria.\n103\t\n104\t## Open Question → Investigation Mapping\n105\t\n106\t| Strategy open question | Investigation | Downstream effect |\n107\t|------------------------|---------------|-------------------|\n108\t| OQ1: Do Kueue's gang-admission semantics (waitForPodsReady) satisfy HLR-1 at target scale, or is scheduler-plugin work needed? | E001 | Gates the HLR-1 implementation (branch slot E003): outcome A → Kueue-native enablement; outcome B → coscheduling plugin integration |\n109\t| OQ2: Is node topology discovery (Tech Preview) mature enough to build on this release? | E007 | Gates HLR-5 (branch slot E008): outcome A → topology-aware placement; outcome B → defer HLR-5, no epics |\n110\t| OQ3: What preemption semantics do reference customers need — full eviction with requeue, or checkpoint-aware graceful preemption? | E004 | Gates the HLR-4 implementation (branch slot E005, plus E006 in branch B): outcome A → eviction+requeue policy; outcome B → graceful preemption + Training Operator checkpoint hooks |\n111\t\n112\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n113\t\n114\t| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Covering epics |\n115\t|-----|----------|------------------------|----------------|\n116\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Multi-node training jobs admitted all-or-nothing; no partial GPU occupation | E001 (Investigation); BRANCH-A-E003 or BRANCH-B-E003 (mutually exclusive implementations) |\n117\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Per-project GPU quota enforced at admission across PyTorchJob and RayJob | E002 |\n118\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Queue position, quota consumption, and admission state visible in Dashboard | E006 |\n119\t| HLR-4 | P1 | Higher-priority workloads preempt lower-priority ones per admin-defined policy | E004 (Investigation); BRANCH-A-E005, or BRANCH-B-E005 + BRANCH-B-E006 |\n120\t| HLR-5 | P2 | Placement prefers GPU-topology-aligned nodes when topology info is exposed | E007 (Investigation); BRANCH-A-E008 |\n121\t\n122\tAll five HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n123\t\n124\t## Conditional Branches\n125\t\n126\t- **E001 (gang admission validation)** — two bounded outcomes:\n127\t  - Branch A (`RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E003`): Kueue-native gang admission enablement.\n128\t    Gate failure impact: rewrite (replaced by scheduler-plugin integration).\n129\t  - Branch B (`RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E003`): coscheduling scheduler-plugin integration.\n130\t    Gate failure impact: rewrite (replaced by Kueue-native enablement).\n131\t- **E004 (preemption semantics)** — two bounded outcomes:\n132\t  - Branch A (`RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E005`): Kueue preemption policy with full eviction\n133\t    and requeue. Gate failure impact: rewrite.\n134\t  - Branch B (`RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E005` + `RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E006`): graceful\n135\t    checkpoint-aware preemption — queueing side plus Training Operator checkpoint hooks.\n136\t    Gate failure impact on E006-slot: remove (no checkpoint hooks needed if eviction\n137\t    semantics are chosen).\n138\t- **E007 (topology discovery maturity)** — two bounded outcomes:\n139\t  - Branch A (`RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008`): topology-aware placement. Gate failure\n140\t    impact: remove (HLR-5 deferred to a future release).\n141\t  - Branch B: no epics — HLR-5 is descoped/deferred; Tier 1 value is unaffected.\n142\t\n143\t## Tiered Delivery\n144\t\n145\tExternal dependency with uncertain timing: node topology discovery (Tech Preview) for HLR-5.\n146\t\n147\t- **Tier 1 (independent partial value)**: HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3, HLR-4 — queue-aware\n148\t  admission, quota, visibility, and preemption all deliverable without topology discovery.\n149\t- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated)**: HLR-5 topology-aware placement — gated by the maturity\n150\t  assessment; if the capability is not mature enough, it is deferred with no impact on\n151\t  Tier 1 delivery.\n152\t\n153\t## Health Warnings\n154\t\n155\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted Teams table,\n156\t   no Dependencies table, no Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then with \"measured by\"\n157\t   clauses), no Non-Functional Requirements, no Technical Approach, and no Staff Engineer\n158\t   Input. Teams were inferred from architecture-context ownership; epic acceptance criteria\n159\t   were derived from the HLRs. A pass over the strategy to add explicit ACs is recommended.\n160\t2. **Affected Components is a flat list** without change descriptions or owner teams.\n161\t   Training Operator is not listed but is implicated by HLR-2 (\"across training job types\")\n162\t   and by checkpoint-aware preemption (open question 3); it is included as a component for\n163\t   the