{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-847107a9a284c146","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate Kueue gang admission for multi-node training jobs at target scale\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate Kueue gang admission for multi-node training jobs at target scale\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's first open question: whether Kueue's current all-or-nothing\n30\tadmission semantics (waitForPodsReady) satisfy the all-or-nothing admission requirement\n31\t(HLR-1) for PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads at the platform's target scale, or whether\n32\tscheduler-plugin work (e.g. coscheduling) beyond Kueue is required. The strategy states\n33\tthis answer \"changes the shape of most implementation work\", so the outcome gates the\n34\tgang-admission implementation and is recorded as a bounded two-outcome decision.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Reproduce all-or-nothing admission behavior for multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob\n39\t  workloads using Kueue's waitForPodsReady semantics, at representative workload sizes\n40\t  (up to the largest supported multi-node GPU job sizes, e.g. 16-GPU-class jobs).\n41\t- Measure partial-occupation windows: how long pods of a pending job can hold GPUs while\n42\t  the remaining pods are unschedulable, and what happens on admission timeout.\n43\t- Identify failure modes relevant to the requirement: partial scheduling, timeout death\n44\t  of partially scheduled jobs, and starvation interactions with other queued workloads.\n45\t- Assess the RayJob admission path through the kuberay/Kueue integration equivalently to\n46\t  the PyTorchJob path.\n47\t- Produce a written go/no-go assessment per job type with an explicit decision criterion:\n48\t  no partial GPU occupation while waiting for the remaining pods, beyond a bounded\n49\t  admission timeout, at target scale.\n50\t- If the assessment is no-go: characterize the gap and scope the scheduler-plugin\n51\t  alternative (e.g. coscheduling) — what integration with the platform scheduler and the\n52\t  Kueue quota/admission model would be required.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A written assessment exists answering the open question for both PyTorchJob and RayJob,\n57\t  with reproducible evidence (test configurations, measurements, environment details).\n58\t- The assessment states a clear bounded decision per job type: (A) Kueue-native\n59\t  waitForPodsReady semantics are sufficient, or (B) scheduler-plugin work beyond Kueue\n60\t  is required.\n61\t- The decision criterion is explicit and measurable (no partial GPU occupation beyond a\n62\t  bounded admission timeout at target scale).\n63\t- If outcome B: the gap analysis is detailed enough to scope the scheduler-plugin\n64\t  integration work without a second discovery pass.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-1 (P0): resolves the gating unknown for all-or-nothing admission of multi-node\n69\t  training jobs; the chosen implementation path (Kueue-native vs scheduler-plugin) is\n70\t  selected by this investigation's outcome.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20c155d45f7e3ee","agent_id":"a16eec3b24d925173","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"412b012b-1336-4d6b-acdf-ce8d33fb83b5","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:37:05.424Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-847107a9a284c146",