{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94043137f5413a56","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n3\ttitle: Determine required preemption semantics and checkpoint overhead\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Determine required preemption semantics and checkpoint overhead\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's third open question for HLR-4: what preemption semantics reference\n30\tcustomers actually need — full eviction with requeue, or checkpoint-aware graceful\n31\tpreemption. The strategy records conflicting field signals and no existing benchmark of\n32\tcheckpoint overhead. This investigation produces a grounded decision plus a measured\n33\tcheckpoint-overhead benchmark, and defines the admin-facing preemption policy\n34\trequirements. The outcome gates the preemption implementation (two bounded outcomes).\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Benchmark checkpoint overhead for representative multi-node PyTorchJob training\n39\t  workloads: checkpoint save time, restart/restore time, and impact on training progress\n40\t  at realistic job sizes.\n41\t- Consolidate field signals on required preemption semantics from reference customers\n42\t  (stakeholder input — this part cannot be resolved from code or docs alone).\n43\t- Produce a recommendation over two bounded outcomes: (A) full eviction with requeue\n44\t  (queueing-layer preemption policy only), or (B) checkpoint-aware graceful preemption\n45\t  (queueing-layer graceful preemption plus training-side checkpoint hooks).\n46\t- Specify the admin-defined preemption policy requirements: priority scheme, which\n47\t  workloads are preemptable, and requeue behavior.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A written decision document selects outcome A or B (or a bounded hybrid, e.g.\n52\t  admin-selectable per queue), with rationale grounded in the benchmark and field input.\n53\t- The checkpoint-overhead benchmark is reproducible and reports save/restore times and\n54\t  throughput impact for representative multi-node training jobs.\n55\t- The admin-defined policy requirements (priority model, preemptability, requeue) are\n56\t  specified precisely enough to implement without a further discovery pass.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-4 (P1): resolves the gating unknown for policy-driven preemption; the chosen\n61\t  semantics decide which preemption implementation is built.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20c155d45f7e3ee","agent_id":"a16eec3b24d925173","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"f030d2c3-593c-46e1-af3a-62833c9ca59c","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:37:07.476Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-94043137f5413a56","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
