{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1a346bc17c28cfe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E006\n3\ttitle: Dashboard visibility for queue position, quota consumption, and admission state\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 8\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Dashboard visibility for queue position, quota consumption, and admission state\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tDelivers HLR-3: users can see queue position, quota consumption, and admission state for\n35\ttheir pending training jobs in the Dashboard. Extends the Dashboard's existing\n36\tdistributed-workload status surfaces. Per the Dashboard architecture context, the\n37\tDashboard reads and writes Kubernetes CRs and owns no data plane — the new views read\n38\tWorkload CRs and queueing status via the Kubernetes API, with no private component APIs.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- New/extended Dashboard views for pending distributed training workloads: queue position,\n43\t  per-project GPU quota consumption, and admission state (pending vs admitted).\n44\t- Navigation and project-scoped presentation consistent with existing Dashboard\n45\t  integration patterns (per-component feature flag via the Dashboard config CR where\n46\t  appropriate).\n47\t- Reads only the Kubernetes API (Workload CRs and queueing status); no new backend\n48\t  service or private API.\n49\t\n50\tThis work builds against the per-project GPU quota model established by the\n51\tquota-enforcement work (the quota-consumption view is scoped by that model), so it is\n52\tsequenced after it. It otherwise runs in parallel with the admission, preemption, and\n53\ttopology tracks: the data it displays (Workload CRs, queue status) is exposed via\n54\texisting Kubernetes APIs regardless of which admission or preemption approach is chosen.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A user can see the queue position of their pending jobs (HLR-3).\n59\t- A user can see their project's GPU quota consumption.\n60\t- A user can see the admission state (pending vs admitted) of their jobs.\n61\t- Views are project-scoped per the Dashboard's RBAC model.\n62\t- End-to-end validation against a cluster with per-project GPU quotas and queue-based\n63\t  admission enabled: displayed queue position, quota consumption, and admission state\n64\t  match the actual queue state.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-3 (P1): full coverage — queue position, quota consumption, and admission state\n69\t  visible in the Dashboard for pending jobs.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20c155d45f7e3ee","agent_id":"a16eec3b24d925173","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"f0588060-6dc1-49cc-b782-fd2e9f78e856","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:37:08.410Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1a346bc17c28cfe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
