{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-839e26f1c3b4350a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E007\n3\ttitle: Assess maturity of node topology discovery for topology-aware placement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Assess maturity of node topology discovery for topology-aware placement\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's second open question for HLR-5: whether node topology discovery —\n30\tcurrently Tech Preview in the platform — is mature enough to build topology-aware job\n31\tplacement on in this release. The outcome gates the topology-aware placement\n32\timplementation: if mature enough, placement work proceeds; if not, HLR-5 is deferred to a\n33\tfuture release with no impact on the rest of the strategy.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Assess the current state of node topology discovery from public/upstream documentation,\n38\t  release notes, and issue trackers: API stability, known issues, upgrade behavior, and\n39\t  support status.\n40\t- Validate actual topology reporting on representative GPU node topologies (e.g. NVLink\n41\t  domains) where hardware is available.\n42\t- Determine compatibility with the platform's queueing/scheduling stack (Kueue-based\n43\t  admission; topology-aware scheduling is Tech Preview per the Distributed Workloads\n44\t  architecture context).\n45\t- Produce a bounded decision: (A) mature enough — proceed with topology-aware placement\n46\t  this release; (B) not mature enough — defer HLR-5.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- A written assessment with a clear go/no-go decision for building on node topology\n51\t  discovery this release.\n52\t- Evidence cited (API versions, known issues, support status, validation results) is\n53\t  sufficient to justify the decision.\n54\t- If no-go: a summary of the maturity gaps and what would change the decision in a\n55\t  future release.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-5 (P2): resolves the gating unknown for topology-aware placement; the decision\n60\t  determines whether the placement implementation is built this release or deferred.\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20c155d45f7e3ee","agent_id":"a16eec3b24d925173","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"d545cd75-6c93-4c89-8a98-6301af6cf854","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:37:09.428Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-839e26f1c3b4350a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
