{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad06b870c5e76a8a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E003\n3\ttitle: Kueue-native gang admission for multi-node training jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the gang-admission validation finds Kueue's waitForPodsReady\n16\t    insufficient at target scale, this epic is replaced by scheduler-plugin (coscheduling)\n17\t    integration for gang admission.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 6\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Kueue-native gang admission for multi-node training jobs\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplements HLR-1 using Kueue's native all-or-nothing admission (waitForPodsReady),\n39\tselected when the gang-admission validation investigation confirms Kueue semantics are\n40\tsufficient at target scale. Multi-node training jobs are admitted all-or-nothing: no\n41\tpartial GPU occupation while waiting for the remaining pods.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Enable and configure Kueue's waitForPodsReady gang-admission semantics for PyTorchJob\n46\t  and RayJob workloads (admission timeout, pods-ready conditions) per the validation\n47\t  findings.\n48\t- Tune admission timeout and requeue behavior for partially-ready jobs so they do not\n49\t  hold GPUs indefinitely (the problem statement's \"12 of 16 GPUs held for hours\" failure\n50\t  mode).\n51\t- Rollback path: because this replaces the existing piecemeal admission behavior, the\n52\t  all-or-nothing semantics must be revertible per-queue via configuration (feature-flag /\n53\t  rollback requirement).\n54\t- Validation at target scale reproducing the validation investigation's decision\n55\t  criterion for both job types.\n56\t- Incidental documentation updates that fall out of this change are included here as\n57\t  scope; no separate documentation work stream.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- A multi-node PyTorchJob (e.g. 16-GPU class) is admitted all-or-nothing: while pending,\n62\t  it holds zero GPUs — no partial GPU occupation while waiting for remaining pods\n63\t  (HLR-1).\n64\t- The same all-or-nothing guarantee holds for RayJob workloads.\n65\t- Partially-unready jobs are evicted and requeued within the configured timeout rather\n66\t  than holding GPUs for hours.\n67\t- Admission semantics can be reverted per-queue via configuration without platform\n68\t  reinstall (rollback / feature flag).\n69\t- Scheduling of non-training workloads is unaffected.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-1 (P0): full coverage on the Kueue-native path (applies when the gang-admission\n74\t  validation selects this outcome).\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20c155d45f7e3ee","agent_id":"a16eec3b24d925173","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"54f66eef-a9d3-4e96-98b6-81ff231e458b","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:37:13.994Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad06b870c5e76a8a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
