roup or\n49\t  not at all, with per-project GPU quota still enforced at admission.\n50\t- Rollback path: the plugin can be disabled per-queue or cluster-wide via configuration,\n51\t  reverting to previous scheduling behavior without reinstall (this replaces existing\n52\t  piecemeal admission behavior).\n53\t- Platform-level review of the scheduler configuration change (deploying a scheduler\n54\t  plugin is a platform-scope change beyond a single component).\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- Multi-node PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads are admitted all-or-nothing: no partial GPU\n59\t  occupation while waiting for remaining pods (HLR-1).\n60\t- Gang admission composes with per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission time.\n61\t- Disabling the plugin reverts to previous scheduling behavior without platform\n62\t  reinstall (rollback / feature flag).\n63\t- No regression to scheduling of non-training workloads.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-1 (P0): full coverage on the scheduler-plugin path (applies when the\n68\t  gang-admission validation selects this outcome).\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20c155d45f7e3ee","agent_id":"a16eec3b24d925173","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"58de29a5-24b0-40c2-9a92-67572340f2bc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:37:14.942Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fd904b2661b3245","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
