 consistency: checkpoint and restore are correct for distributed\n52\t  (multi-node, multi-GPU) jobs.\n53\t- Coordination with the graceful-preemption protocol defined by the queueing-side work\n54\t  in the same branch (signal semantics, grace period, checkpoint location).\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A preempted multi-node PyTorchJob saves a usable checkpoint within the grace period.\n59\t- On re-admission, the job restores from the checkpoint and training progresses correctly\n60\t  (no loss beyond the checkpoint interval).\n61\t- Checkpoint save and restore times are within the bounds characterized by the\n62\t  preemption-semantics investigation's benchmark.\n63\t- Jobs that do not opt into checkpointing are unaffected (graceful preemption degrades to\n64\t  plain eviction for them).\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-4 (P1): training-side coverage on the graceful path (applies when the\n69\t  preemption-semantics investigation selects checkpoint-aware graceful semantics).\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b20c155d45f7e3ee","agent_id":"a16eec3b24d925173","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"7878187e-dd90-4633-ba9a-e9f7e4c5a8eb","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:37:18.415Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-897e89f3ae9a3679","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9005 decomposition"}
