{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad5cd8d2e57b2689","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-E002\n3\ttitle: Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission for training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Per-project GPU quota enforcement at admission for training workloads\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDelivers HLR-2: per-project GPU quota is enforced at admission time across training job\n34\ttypes (PyTorchJob, RayJob). Built on the platform's existing Kueue-based queueing model\n35\t(ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model per the Distributed Workloads architecture context).\n36\tA job whose project has exhausted its GPU quota is queued rather than partially scheduled.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Define and implement the per-project GPU quota model for training workloads using the\n41\t  existing Kueue quota machinery (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue).\n42\t- Ensure both PyTorchJob and RayJob workloads are subject to queue admission and counted\n43\t  against their project's GPU quota — PyTorchJob via the existing Kueue integration;\n44\t  RayJob via the kuberay integration (validate and close any gaps so both job types are\n45\t  quota-subject).\n46\t- Administrative configuration of per-project GPU quota values without code changes.\n47\t- Incidental documentation updates that fall out of this change (quota configuration\n48\t  references) are included here as scope; no separate documentation work stream.\n49\t\n50\tThis work is independent of the gang-admission semantics question (all-or-nothing\n51\tadmission): quota enforcement applies at Kueue admission either way, so it proceeds in\n52\tparallel with that investigation and its follow-on implementation.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- A job submitted to a project whose GPU quota is exhausted is not admitted (remains\n57\t  pending in queue) rather than partially scheduled — for both PyTorchJob and RayJob\n58\t  (HLR-2).\n59\t- Quota consumption accounts for GPU resources across both training job types within a\n60\t  project (a PyTorchJob and a RayJob in the same project draw from the same quota).\n61\t- Demonstrated test: an over-quota job stays queued while quota is held by admitted jobs;\n62\t  when capacity is released, the pending job is admitted.\n63\t- Per-project GPU quota is configurable by an administrator without code changes.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-2 (P0): full coverage — per-project GPU quota enforced at admission time across\n68\t  training job types.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9a97bac5b606333","agent_id":"aa5c7adac137312cd","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"9ed75aa3-5531-414a-8c33-8d639923fba0","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:47:56.347Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad5cd8d2e57b2689","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
