\n50\t  preemption-semantics investigation.\n51\t- Integration of the grace/checkpoint protocol with the per-project GPU quota model on\n52\t  re-admission.\n53\t- If the queueing layer's native hooks are insufficient for graceful preemption,\n54\t  coordinate the required upstream contribution.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- On preemption per the admin-defined policy, a training job receives a checkpoint signal\n59\t  and a bounded grace period before eviction (HLR-4).\n60\t- The preempted job is requeued and, on re-admission, resumes from its checkpoint\n61\t  (restore is completed by the training-side checkpoint hooks).\n62\t- Checkpoint overhead stays within the bounds characterized by the preemption-semantics\n63\t  investigation's benchmark.\n64\t- The preemption policy is admin-configurable without code changes.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-4 (P1): queueing-side coverage on the graceful path (applies when the\n69\t  preemption-semantics investigation selects this outcome; training-side coverage is\n70\t  provided by the PyTorchJob checkpoint hooks in the same branch).\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9a97bac5b606333","agent_id":"aa5c7adac137312cd","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"0ea2afdc-55eb-422e-9a2f-b9ae9cede8f9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:48:10.151Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aff33d1dbc93e799","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
