{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e59cf86cab69bc6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E006\n3\ttitle: PyTorchJob checkpoint hooks for graceful preemption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Training Operator\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E004\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-B-E005\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If checkpoint-aware graceful preemption semantics are not chosen,\n17\t    this epic is removed entirely.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# PyTorchJob checkpoint hooks for graceful preemption\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tImplements the training side of checkpoint-aware graceful preemption for HLR-4 in the\n39\tTraining Operator: PyTorchJob workloads respond to a preemption-triggered checkpoint\n40\tsignal by saving state within the bounded grace period, and restore from the checkpoint\n41\twhen the requeued job is re-admitted. Selected when the preemption-semantics\n42\tinvestigation chooses graceful semantics.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Checkpoint-on-signal support for PyTorchJob: on graceful-preemption notification, the\n47\t  job's workers save a checkpoint within the bounded grace period defined by the\n48\t  queueing-side graceful preemption work.\n49\t- Restore-on-restart: when the requeued job is re-admitted, training resumes from the\n50\t  latest checkpoint.\n51\t- Multi-node consistency: checkpoint and restore are correct for distributed\n52\t  (multi-node, multi-GPU) jobs.\n53\t- Coordination with the graceful-preemption protocol defined by the queueing-side work\n54\t  in the same branch (signal semantics, grace period, checkpoint location).\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A preempted multi-node PyTorchJob saves a usable checkpoint within the grace period.\n59\t- On re-admission, the job restores from the checkpoint and training progresses correctly\n60\t  (no loss beyond the checkpoint interval).\n61\t- Checkpoint save and restore times are within the bounds characterized by the\n62\t  preemption-semantics investigation's benchmark.\n63\t- Jobs that do not opt into checkpointing are unaffected (graceful preemption degrades to\n64\t  plain eviction for them).\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-4 (P1): training-side coverage on the graceful path (applies when the\n69\t  preemption-semantics investigation selects checkpoint-aware graceful semantics).\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9a97bac5b606333","agent_id":"aa5c7adac137312cd","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"00739560-be7f-42a5-ab12-65748597c8fa","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:48:11.230Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e59cf86cab69bc6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
