{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b5670628af97475","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9005-BRANCH-A-E008\n3\ttitle: Topology-aware job placement for GPU training workloads\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9005\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9005-E007\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9005-E007\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If node topology discovery is assessed as not mature enough for\n16\t    this release, HLR-5 is deferred and this epic is removed.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 4\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Topology-aware job placement for GPU training workloads\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tImplements HLR-5: job placement prefers GPU-topology-aligned nodes (e.g. within NVLink\n38\tdomains rather than crossing them) when the cluster exposes topology information.\n39\tSelected when the topology-discovery maturity assessment is a go for this release.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Enable topology-aware placement in the queueing/scheduling layer (building on the\n44\t  Tech Preview topology-aware scheduling capability of the platform's queueing stack) so\n45\t  multi-node GPU jobs prefer topology-aligned nodes when topology information is\n46\t  available.\n47\t- Graceful degradation: when the cluster does not expose topology information, placement\n48\t  falls back to current behavior with no regression.\n49\t- Validation on topology-exposing GPU nodes demonstrating measurably better placement\n50\t  (jobs not crossing NVLink domains where an aligned placement exists).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- When topology information is exposed, pending multi-node GPU jobs are placed on\n55\t  topology-aligned nodes in preference to misaligned ones (HLR-5).\n56\t- When topology information is absent, scheduling behaves as before (no regression).\n57\t- Placement preference is demonstrable on a topology-exposing cluster (aligned placement\n58\t  chosen where feasible).\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-5 (P2): full coverage on the proceed path (applies when the topology-discovery\n63\t  maturity assessment selects this outcome).\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a9a97bac5b606333","agent_id":"aa5c7adac137312cd","session_id":"1a3bc56e-6837-46b2-9ccd-e7e0a4b10d8c","uuid":"517943ec-2838-494f-8f97-024186facb51","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:48:12.097Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b5670628af97475","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9005"}
